<cell id="cell-12"><cell_type>markdown</cell_type>## Architecture (Mermaid)

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    S[STARStory<br/>Situation / Task<br/>Action / Result] --> LIB[STARLibrary<br/>add / by_tag / by_role / by_bank]
    LIB --> P[principles_covered<br/>tag_for_principle]
    P --> PR[LeadershipPrinciple<br/>vision / execution /<br/>collab / tech / mentor]
    LIB --> M[match_stories<br/>question -> top-3]
    MOCK[MockQuestion<br/>30 common questions] --> M
    LIB --> SC[score_story<br/>quant / clear / impact / dur / role]
    S --> R[Rehearsal<br/>3-min / 2-min / 1-min]
    SC --> R
```

**Read as:** Stories go into the library; the library is indexed by tag, role, bank, and principle. Questions flow in; the matcher returns the top-3 stories. Each story has a 3-2-1 rehearsal and a heuristic score.</cell id="cell-12">
<cell id="cell-13"><cell_type>markdown</cell_type>## Reflect (10 min)

1. Why does the heuristic scorer weight `result_quantified` so heavily? What is the interviewer actually listening for?
2. The match_stories function scores keyword overlap. What happens when two stories have the same keywords but one is from 5 years ago and the other is from 6 months ago? Should the scorer care?
3. The 3-2-1 framework says every story needs three layers of compression. What's the failure mode if you only have the 3-min version?
4. The library has 8 stories covering all 5 banks and all 5 principles. Is that enough for a principal loop? What would you add for the L8 band?
5. (Stretch) The `tag_for_principle` heuristic uses keyword matching. Write a story that covers VISION but doesn't contain any of the VISION keywords. How would you redesign the tagger to catch it?

